// The decoder attention layer of tests/boundary/onnx_bounded_kv_fixture.py
// with a past bounded by 8, as udoncl-lower-onnx-to-host leaves it. The
// fused kernels index at the largest extents and take the value of `past`
// (and the pitch of every bound graph input or output they read or write)
// as i32 scalars after their buffers:
//
// - present = Concat(past, new) is written with the pitch of its binding;
//   the split between past and new is the run-time extent of past. The key
//   and the value share the kernel.
// - The padding of the mask and the scaled transposed keys are dense at
//   their run-time extents (past + 1).
// - The Softmax of the masked scores loops to the run-time extent.
// - Every element past the extent is written as zero without a Load.

